<%# Which session the set is going into, and what was just put in it. #631.

    The form had no heading, so nothing on it said which session it was adding to, and saving
    went to a read-only page with nowhere onward. It comes back here now, and the line below
    says what landed, with the way back to the workout for when the session is all in. From the
    session screen the form still goes back to the session instead, as #578 made it. %>
<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
  Add a set to <%= [@workout.label, @workout.performed_or_planned_on.strftime('%A %-d %B')].compact.join(', ') %>
</h1>
<%- if @set_notice %>
  <p class="mt-3 rounded-md bg-amber-50 p-3 text-sm text-amber-900 ring-1 ring-amber-200" role="alert"><%= @set_notice %></p>
<%- end %>
<%- if @just_saved %>
  <p class="mt-3 rounded-md bg-emerald-100 p-3 text-sm text-emerald-900 ring-1 ring-emerald-900/25" role="status">
    Saved <%= @just_saved.exercise.name %>, <%= load_label(@just_saved) %>. Add the next one below, or
    <a href="/workouts/<%= @workout.id %>/" class="font-semibold underline">go back to the workout</a>.
  </p>
<%- end %>
<div class="mt-6">
  <%== render('sets/_form') %>
</div>
